      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Balmain Rugby Football Club, founded in 1873, captured its first premiership just two years later in 1875, making it one of Australia’s oldest clubs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balmain%2C_New_South_Wales",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Balmain Association, established in 1965, safeguards the suburb’s heritage and keeps its archives at the Watch House on Darling Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://balmainassociation.org.au/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Dawn Fraser Pool, once called Elkington Park Baths, was renamed in 1964 to honor the Olympic champion who grew up in Balmain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
